---
.title = "Ask structured questions with Decision",
.description = "Send a state and typed questions to LLMD, use conditional questions, and read scored labels.",
.date = .date("2026-11-18T00:00:00"),
.layout = "content.shtml",
.custom = .{ .doc_section = "Tutorials" },
---
Send a shared state and typed questions to `POST /v1/systemone`. LLMD returns
a scored label for each question it answers. This example classifies an animal,
asks a follow-up for cats, and rates playfulness on a three-label scale.

# [Send a Decision request]($heading.id('send-a-decision-request'))

In the [Decision catalog]($link.page('llmd/reference/model-compatibility').unsafeRef('decision-checkpoints')),
choose `LiquidAI/LFM3-1.7B` and your backend, then choose **Configure launch**.
The catalog also lists the StartLux Decision v1.1 Instant and AutoThink
models. Use the generated commands to start LLMD
and check the loaded model with `GET /v1/models`.

Explore either animal answer below. To try the request, run it in a second
terminal. It uses port `8000`. The generated request uses the port you select.

```=html
<div class="decision-example" data-toc-parent="send-a-decision-request">
  <section class="decision-map" aria-labelledby="follow-the-decision">
    <h3 id="follow-the-decision" data-toc-label="Follow the decision">Follow the decision</h3>
    <fieldset class="command-tabs">
      <legend>Simulated animal answer</legend>
      <label class="command-tab"><input type="radio" name="decision-animal" value="cat" checked><span>Cat</span></label>
      <label class="command-tab"><input type="radio" name="decision-animal" value="dog"><span>Dog</span></label>
    </fieldset>
    <div class="decision-node"><strong><code>animal</code></strong><span>Which animal is it?</span></div>
    <div class="decision-gate"><code>ask_if</code></div>
    <div class="decision-branches">
      <div class="decision-branch" data-animal="cat">
        <strong>Cat</strong>
        <div class="decision-node"><strong><code>cute</code></strong><span>Ask “Is it cute?”</span></div>
      </div>
      <div class="decision-branch" data-animal="dog">
        <strong>Dog</strong>
        <div class="decision-node"><strong><code>cute</code></strong><span>Skip this question</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="decision-node decision-rating"><strong><code>rating</code></strong><span>Eligible on both paths</span></div>
    <p class="decision-context" role="status" aria-atomic="true"><code>depends_on</code> ·
      <span data-context="cat">With cat, <code>rating</code> receives the <code>cute</code> label when available.</span>
      <span data-context="dog">With dog, <code>cute</code> is skipped. <code>rating</code> can still run without its label.</span>
    </p>
  </section>
  <div class="command-shell" id="decision-request" data-toc-label="Copyable request">
    <span class="command-language icon-code">Shell · POST /v1/systemone</span>
    <pre><code class="sh" data-copy-label="Copy Decision request">curl -sS --fail-with-body http://127.0.0.1:8000/v1/systemone \
  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
  -d '{
    "state": "The animal sits on the mat, purrs and chases a red laser dot.",
    "questions": {
      "animal": {"kind": "choice", "instructions": "Which animal is it?", "criteria": {"cat": null, "dog": "barks"}},
      "cute":   {"kind": "noul", "instructions": "Is it cute?", "ask_if": {"animal": ["cat"]}},
      "rating": {"kind": "score", "instructions": "How playful is it?", "criteria": ["low", "medium", "high"], "depends_on": ["cute"]}
    }
  }'
</code></pre>
  </div>
</div>
```

Append `| jq .` to format a successful JSON response if you have jq installed.

# [Read the answers]($heading.id('read-the-answers'))

The `answers` object uses the question IDs from your request.

- `answers.animal.label` is `"cat"` or `"dog"` when the question succeeds.
  The optional description `"barks"` gives the model context for the dog label.
- `cute` runs only when `animal` returns `"cat"`. A `noul` answer is the string
  `"true"` or `"false"`. When the condition fails, the entry is `{"skipped":true}`.
- `rating` runs after `cute`. Its prompt includes the earlier label when
  available. If `cute` was skipped, `rating` can still return `"low"`,
  `"medium"`, or `"high"`. To rate only cats, add
  `"ask_if": {"animal": ["cat"]}` to `rating`.

Check each entry for `error` or `skipped` before reading its label and
scores. See the [Decision API reference]($link.page('llmd/reference/v1/systemone').ref('decision'))
for label probabilities, token usage, and request validation.
